invariant: INV-22
file: srv_tcp_nonblocking.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_srv_record_in keeps taking records after the one that completed
  the handshake. A client that sends its first application record in the
  same segment as its Finished, as h2spec does with its HTTP/2 preface,
  then sees the server feed that record to the finished handshake and die
  with unexpected_message, and a caller cannot split the bytes at the
  handshake's end without parsing records itself. test/tcp_nonblocking_coalesced_tests.h
  delivers the Finished and one application record in one call and
  requires the record to reach ch_read.

--- old
        if (r->step == SRV_TCP_NONBLOCKING_STEP_COMPLETE) {
            return CH_OK;
        }
--- new
        (void)SRV_TCP_NONBLOCKING_STEP_COMPLETE;
